// FIXED by the rtype write-back (setup_static_bind unifies the
// instance's settled rtype into the site's LIVE rtype cell; abstract
// returns retry through privatize_type and skip when still opaque).
// Both engines now read the elem union [i64, fn]: the map de-fuses
// and the comparison runs on real values in both modes.
// Originally: aug08c katana fuzz/000000, 2026-08-08.
// ROOT-CAUSED 2026-08-08 (v2 — the union_identical guess was WRONG):
// a REC def's call-site rtype cell is SEVERED from the body's
// inferred return. Reduction matrix (all verified):
//   rec + inner lambda call        -> DIVERGES  (t5)
//   rec + destructure inner call   -> DIVERGES  (t6; destructure
//                                     irrelevant)
//   no-rec + inner call            -> AGREE     (t4 — elem reads fn,
//                                     map de-fuses)
//   rec, call rtype ANNOTATED i64  -> SOUND compile error "i64 does
//                                     not contain fn" AT THE DEF BODY
//                                     (t7 — annotation binds before
//                                     the tc1 resolve)
// Mechanism: `let rec f = |n,acc| { let g = |v| array::iter; g(x) }`
// has an UNBOUND def rtype at def-gate end (the body's return is an
// inner CALL, which resolves at typecheck1). The outer `f(...)` site
// freshens (is_rec_self_call only knots sites inside the def check),
// so the site rtype is fresh-unbound at its typecheck1. There
// `setup_static_bind` snapshots `self.ftype.resolve_tvars()` — a
// DEEP CLONE — and the instance body re-drive binds the fn into the
// SNAPSHOT's rtype cell; the site's live cell stays unbound (the
// non-rec path flows the fn back to the site — t4/t8 prove it — the
// rec path does not). A LATER tc1 constraint then binds the orphaned
// site cell freely: here `array::map`'s callback cmp `x > i64:3`
// unifies the elem union [i64, 'site_rtype] with i64, binding
// 'site_rtype := i64. Nothing re-checks. Static type Array<i64>,
// runtime element = the fn value: the kernel soundly freezes i64 and
// reads the wrong-family slot as placeholder 0 (false); the interp
// compares the real fn (> 3 = true, Value total order).
// FIX DIRECTION (Eric's call): either outer calls to a rec def share
// the def's cells (monomorphic recursion made total — matches the
// 2026-07-06 ruling), or the instance re-drive must unify the
// instance's settled rtype back into the site's live cell.
{let a = [i64:0, i64:0, {let rec f = |n, acc| {type T = {bar: i64, baz: f64, foo: Array<f64>}; let x = { bar: i64:42, baz: f64:84., foo: [f64:1., f64:2., f64:4.3, f64:55.23] }; let f = |{bar: bar, ..}: T| array::iter; f(x)}; f(i64:0, buffer::to_string)}, i64:-100, i64:0]; array::map(a, |x| x > i64:3)}
// minimized:
{let a = [i64:0, i64:0, {let rec f = |n, acc| {type T = {bar: i64, baz: f64, foo: Array<f64>}; let x = { bar: i64:0, baz: f64:84., foo: [f64:1., f64:2., f64:4.3, f64:55.23] }; let f = |{bar: bar, ..}: T| array::iter; f(x)}; f(i64:0, buffer::to_string)}, i64:-100, i64:0]; array::map(a, |x| x > i64:3)}
